          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win rounds by emptying your hand (domino) or having the lowest pip count when the game is blocked. First to reach the target score (100 in two-player or partnership, 61 in three or four-handed) wins the game.',
          gameplay: "Tiles are laid end to end matching suits. Player to dealer's left leads. Each turn: play two tiles (one on each end of the line), or if unable and boneyard not empty draw one tile and pass, or if boneyard empty and one tile left play that tile on either end, or if boneyard empty and cannot play then pass. Anyone may call blocked game; hands are then scored. Round ends when someone dominoes, blocked game is called, or everyone has passed.",
          keyRules: [
            'Play exactly two tiles per turn (one on each end of the line), except when boneyard is empty and you have only one tile.',
            'If you cannot play and boneyard is not empty, draw one tile and pass.',
            "Lowest pip total in hand at round end wins the round; winner receives sum of losers' totals minus own total. Tie for lowest: no score.",
            'Game to 100 points (two-player or partnership) or 61 points (three or four-handed).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize playing two tiles that keep both ends of the line flexible; avoid leaving a single suit dominant on one end.',
          intermediate: 'Count suits; know which pip values are likely unavailable on the ends. If the lead was 3-4, 3 and 4 may be scarce. Decide when to call blocked game to maximize opponent penalty.',
          advanced: 'Strategize so both ends change each play; use suit counting to force blocks when it benefits you. Call blocked game to keep scores lower when advantageous.',
          tips: [
            'Both ends change on each successful play, so planning ahead is hard; focus on which suits will not be on the ends.',
            'Calling blocked game stops play and scores hands; use it to limit how high scores get.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
